<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casimir IV Jagiellon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1427">1427</a>–<a href="/years/1492">1492</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Casimir IV of Poland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Casimir IV Jagiellon was Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1440 and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1447. He backed the Prussian Confederation against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, and the Thirteen Years' War ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn">Second Peace of Thorn</a> in 1466, which gave Poland Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. He also abolished the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> in 1471, and his sons ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/casimir-iv-jagiellon.jpg" alt="Casimir IV Jagiellon" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazimier_Jagaj%C5%82avi%C4%8D._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%B7%D1%96%D0%BC%D0%B5%D1%80_%D0%AF%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D1%96%D1%87_(1645).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
